WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:00.120 --> 00:03.820
Our well-being is the foundation of our energy.

2
00:03.880 --> 00:07.340
This energy fuels us across all dimensions —

3
00:07.400 --> 00:15.820
work, learning, performance, awareness,
and the choices we make.

4
00:16.120 --> 00:22.380
When you're in a place of optimal well-being,
things tend to flow smoothly and feel balanced.

5
00:22.840 --> 00:25.820
You're more prepared to take on
whatever comes your way,

6
00:25.880 --> 00:31.580
whether it's learning a new skill,
performing a difficult task,

7
00:32.440 --> 00:40.220
reserving judgment in a difficult conversation,
or quickly executing a deliverable with a tight timeline.

8
00:40.360 --> 00:45.500
But when your well-being is depleted,
it becomes harder to accomplish any of those things,

9
00:45.560 --> 00:48.760
and harder to handle difficulties well.

10
00:48.820 --> 00:55.480
For example, a stressful situation may quickly fill your mind
with anxious or even irrational thoughts.

11
00:55.540 --> 00:59.240
Your heart may start to pound,
and your jaw may clench.

12
00:59.300 --> 01:06.680
The inertia of your default tendency takes over,
and there's much less performing, learning and feeling positive.

13
01:07.460 --> 01:10.680
Stress is not a bad thing in and of itself.

14
01:10.740 --> 01:16.680
It's the accumulation of it at the extreme
that makes it hard for us to be and do our best.

15
01:16.740 --> 01:21.960
Surprisingly, too little stress can also
have a negative impact on your well-being.

16
01:22.020 --> 01:29.080
If you're feeling bored or disengaged,
it's hard to find the energy to power yourself through to a desired outcome.

17
01:29.184 --> 01:34.644
When it comes to your well-being,
the optimal place to be is at the top of the U.

18
01:34.704 --> 01:42.084
With no stimulation or stress at all,
you could end up feeling bored and fail to expand your capacity for growth.

19
01:42.384 --> 01:47.844
On the other hand, when you're overwhelmed
or overly stressed for an extended period of time,

20
01:47.904 --> 01:50.644
you could find yourself in the burnout zone.

21
01:50.704 --> 01:58.884
This can also create a vicious cycle if you shift into survival mode,
which can perpetuate burnout and make it harder to recover.

22
01:59.104 --> 02:04.964
In the cases of both boredom and burnout,
we tend to be less productive, avoid challenges,

23
02:05.024 --> 02:08.564
and miss opportunities to learn and change.

24
02:09.174 --> 02:16.234
At the top of the U, we're experiencing the optimal amount of stress
to maximize our performance and well-being.

25
02:16.294 --> 02:20.714
Our awareness is at its peak,
we're more in control of our responses,

26
02:20.774 --> 02:24.154
and we're primed to make better, positive choices.

27
02:24.374 --> 02:28.154
Staying at the top of the U requires active attention.

28
02:28.214 --> 02:32.154
When we manage our well-being,
we're better able to manage our stress.

29
02:32.214 --> 02:36.554
And by actively managing our stress levels,
we improve our well-being.

30
02:36.694 --> 02:41.594
Though stressful things can't be avoided,
we can change how we handle and cope with them

31
02:41.654 --> 02:47.114
in ways that help us recover our well-being
and enhance our awareness and learning.

32
02:47.174 --> 02:52.432
By doing these things we're able to help ourselves
in both the short and long term.

33
02:52.492 --> 02:55.872
Don't worry if you can't always be at the top of the U.

34
02:55.932 --> 02:59.872
Inevitably, there will be times
when you slide into boredom or burnout.

35
02:59.932 --> 03:01.552
It's part of life.

36
03:01.612 --> 03:10.292
Continually building your awareness of where you are
is part of what will improve your ability to adjust as needed.
